# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=confluence spec=druid:guardian style=good
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
# 10-normal is progress.ts's first rung, open on a fresh save with no
# unlock trick needed. boss=confluence is a coverage label only -- `evening`
# steers at no boss (direction.md's own repeated note) -- so this walks in
# at the door same as any other.
#
# This exact spec/style/size/difficulty (druid:guardian, good, 10-normal,
# mode=clear) already opened [[#6]]'s VIGIL-stall line on 2026-09-25 (two
# convergent runs, wander and good, both stalling within a dozen units of
# each other). Re-running the same corridor confirmation for a fifteenth
# time is not new by itself, so what this session actually tries is
# something no [[#6]] report has checked yet: what the CITADEL map screen
# (README's "the map is a map... the one thing you can still press on it is
# a lit pad") actually shows a player mid-evening, reached via the fight
# screen's own corner `map` button (src/main.ts:2303, `walkingAnEvening()`
# gate) -- whether that is while still crossing, or once a corridor has
# stalled. No session in direction.md has pressed it during a live evening;
# every citadel-screen mention on record is from the class screen's own
# BACK. If VIGIL stalls again as expected, this checks whether the map
# offers any lit room or a GIVE UP a stuck player could actually use, which
# is the practical half of the VIGIL question the fault alone does not
# answer.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:druid:guardian
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening good 200 8
state
shot after-evening
says
bill

tap map
waitscreen citadel 10
shot citadel-view
targets
state
tap back
state
shot after-back
